Add SEO/AEO technical foundation and structured data

Nothing on the site had canonical URLs, Open Graph/Twitter tags, a
sitemap, or any structured data, despite five FAQ accordions across
the site that were pure missed answer-engine opportunity.

- astro.config.mjs: set `site`, add @astrojs/sitemap
- public/robots.txt + public/llms.txt (the latter for AI crawlers/
  answer engines, in the informal but increasingly-recognised format)
- BaseLayout: canonical link, OG/Twitter meta, sitewide Organization
  + WebSite JSON-LD
- src/components/seo/FaqSchema.astro: FAQPage JSON-LD, wired into
  every page with a real FAQ accordion (homepage, the three
  /ai-automation/* service pages, AI Powered Reviews)
- src/components/seo/ServiceSchema.astro: Service JSON-LD per
  offering; AI Powered Reviews also carries a live Offer/price read
  from the page's own LAUNCH_OFFER logic so it can't drift from what
  is actually displayed. Atlas deliberately gets none of this beyond
  the sitewide Organization markup, since it is explicitly
  concept-stage — marking it up as an available product would
  misrepresent that.
- Homepage <title> was literally "Home — Amplio Systems"; replaced
  with an actual descriptive title. lang now en-GB.

